# SeePat — every environment variable this repository reads.
#
# Copy to `.env` (nothing reads `.env.example` itself), or put machine-local
# overrides in `.env.local`, which is git-ignored and wins over `.env`.
#
# There are no secrets in this repository to put in either file: no server, no
# payment gateway, no AI service. Every value below is either a public URL or a
# path on this machine.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THE APP — read by Vite at build time (src/, index.html, vite.config.ts)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The origin the app is deployed to, with NO trailing slash.
#
# Its only job is to make the social-card URLs absolute: index.html builds them
# as `%VITE_SITE_URL%/og-image.png`. Empty is a deliberate, valid state — the
# tags then fall back to root-relative paths, which Twitter, Slack and WhatsApp
# resolve correctly (Facebook does not). A wrong hardcoded domain is worse than
# no domain, because it hands the card to somebody else's server.
#
#   local dev:   leave empty
#   production:  https://seepat.ph
VITE_SITE_URL=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REPO TOOLING — optional. Nothing here is needed to run, test or build the app.
# Only the promo-video pipeline reads these, and every one has a working default,
# so an empty value and an unset variable mean the same thing.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ffmpeg binary used by tools/build-video.mjs.
# Default: the ffmpeg-static copy under the system temp folder.
# FFMPEG=

# Licensed background track for the promo cuts.
# Default: docs/video/music/track-644.mp3
# MUSIC=

# Output basename for the two promo cuts, which land as
# docs/video/<NAME>_1080x1920.mp4 and _1920x1080.mp4. Default: SeePat_promo
# VIDEO_NAME=

# Voice used by tools/make-narration-kokoro.mjs (a Kokoro voice id).
# Default: af_heart
# KOKORO_VOICE=
